# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS
#
# This repo is PUBLIC. Everything below is a credential that would compromise
# either the game server or the AWS account, and none of it belongs in git under
# any circumstances. A secret-scanning gate backs this up on every commit --
# .gitignore is the first line, not the only one.
#
# Where these actually live:
#   AWS            -> the EC2 instance IAM role. There is no key file.
#   Discord OAuth  -> environment, on the Ringmaster host
#   session secret -> environment, on the Ringmaster host
#   ingest secret  -> environment on both hosts
#   SSH key        -> the Ringmaster host only, never checked in
#
# There is deliberately no RCON password in that list. `rcon_password` stays
# unset on the game host, which is FXServer's own default. See the README.
#
# (The backticks above are load-bearing: check-secrets.mjs flags that token
# followed by whitespace, and prose about it trips the rule. Quoting the token
# is the right fix; loosening the rule is not.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# THE DISPATCH KEY, WHICH EVERY PATTERN ABOVE MISSES. It is named `dispatch`
# with no extension -- not *.pem, not *.key, not id_ed25519* -- and it lives at
# .ssh/dispatch inside this checkout on the Ringmaster host. So the file the
# SECRETS note above calls "never checked in" was untracked but NOT ignored,
# which is the one state `git add -A` publishes. check-secrets.mjs flagged it
# for exactly that reason: it scans tracked files plus untracked-and-not-ignored
# ones, because those are the files git would actually publish.
.ssh/
credentials
.aws/

# Working memory, not documentation. Session handoff notes -- the README is the
# documentation, and PLAN.md is deliberately allowed to be messy and current.
# Same convention as the gamemode repo.
PLAN.md

# Agent worktrees. `git worktree add` leaves a directory with its own .git file,
# which `git add -A` from the main checkout commits as an EMBEDDED REPO -- a
# gitlink to a commit that exists nowhere the remote can see. That happened once
# in the gamemode repo and the commit had to be rebuilt. Same convention here.
.worktrees/

# The gamemode checkout CI clones so `check:verdict` has the game's real
# verdict reader to run against. Never committed here — it is another repo, and
# a copy of it in this one would be the exact duplication that check exists to
# catch. See scripts/check-verdict-contract.mjs.
.gamemode/

# Local overrides
*.local
config.local.*

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

